4.0.0 (unreleased):
    * BC PHP 8.1 dropped, minimum version is now PHP 8.2
    * BC Symfony 6 dropped, add Symfony 8 support
    * BC Remove constructors from Interfaces (Liskov Substitution Principle violation)
    * BC Added QueryInterface::selectPrimary()
    * Fix collections and hydrators no longer Countable since 4.0.0-rc.1: count($collection) threw a TypeError
    * BC Remove the Services container, ContainerInterface and the pimple/pimple suggestion: wiring belongs to the integration (ting_bundle)
    * BC Replace the abandoned doctrine/cache with Symfony Cache Contracts: caches are Symfony\Contracts\Cache\CacheInterface pools, Ting\Cache\Cache only exposes get() and delete()
    * Fix UnitOfWork::detach() raising an "Undefined array key" warning when the entity was not queued
    * Fix changing a primary key: the UPDATE / DELETE targeted `WHERE key IN (old, new)` instead of the old value, and ignored a custom getter on primary keys
    * BC Fix Util\Debug, broken by typed properties since 4.0.0-rc.1: objects are now exported as arrays with a __CLASS__ key
    * Fix HydratorValueObject on cached queries (a cache hit returned raw rows): the hydrator now builds the objects itself, from the rows, with or without cache; ResultInterface::setObjectToFetch(), added in 4.0.0-rc.1, is removed
    * Fix cached prepared queries ignoring selectPrimary(true): they were always prepared on a replica
    * Fix UnitOfWork keeping a saved entity queued when it had no change: shouldBePersisted() stayed true and the entity was retained until detach/reset (leak in worker mode)
    * Fix Hydrator::objectSchemaIs() ignored with PostgreSQL since 4.0.0-rc.1: the schema read from the query, even empty, took precedence; objectSchemaIs() overrides it again, as in 3.x
    * Fix Mysqli prepared queries binding NULL for every parameter since 4.0.0-rc.1 (regression of ccmbenchmark/ting#108: parameter order lost, a repeated parameter bound once)
    * Fix a missing query parameter: every driver now raises a QueryException, prepared or not (Pgsql and Mysqli prepared queries sent NULL)
    * Fix the escaped colon (\:) kept in non-prepared Mysqli queries
    * BC Remove Query\Cached\Query::setVersion(): it had no effect, the version is not part of the cache key since cache keys are manual
    * Ting\Cache\Cache used before setCache() now throws a ConfigException instead of an Error on an uninitialized property
    * Fix drivers used without ConnectionPool: a TypeError when no name (Mysqli, Pgsql) or no database (Mysqli) had been set; both default to an empty string
    * BC Remove the unused SerializerFactoryInterface argument from RepositoryFactory::__construct() (already removed from Repository::__construct() in 4.0.0-rc.1, now documented)
    * Fix connections without user or password (optional since 3.x) failing with a TypeError since 4.0.0-rc.1: DriverInterface::connect() accepts null; Pgsql leaves them out of the DSN so libpq uses its defaults
    * Fix Pgsql reads of a column without table (function, VALUES, CTE...) failing with a TypeError since 4.0.0-rc.1
    * Fix Pgsql Driver::execute() logging the rewritten SQL ($1) instead of the query with its named parameters since 4.0.0-rc.1
    * Fix Pgsql Driver::execute() never stopping the query log when the query fails
    * Fix Mysqli prepared queries without result set (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE) returning false on success since 4.0.0-rc.1; they return true again, as Pgsql
    * Fix Serializer\BackedEnum::serialize() returning an int for an int-backed enum since 4.0.0-rc.1; it returns a string again, as in 3.x
    * Fix MetadataRepository registering an empty entity for a metadata without entity (PHP 8.5 deprecation "Using null as an array offset", '' listed by getAllEntities())
    * Fix Pgsql Statement destructor: no DEALLOCATE without connection, and no Error thrown from the destructor when the connection was closed (close(), reconnect())
    * Fix HydratorAggregator dropping the last group when the last row belonged to a group already yielded; the last group is keyed and built from its first row, like the others
    * Fix UnitOfWork updates and deletes sending the primary key of the WHERE clause without its serializer: an enum or DateTime key reached the driver as an object (error), a serializer whose output differs from __toString() matched no row; this includes primary keys whose serializer comes from their type (datetime, uuid, json...), which never got it
    * Fix the columns of the WHERE clause of get(), getBy() and getOneBy() not being escaped (reserved words such as "order" made invalid SQL; PostgreSQL lowercased mixed-case columns), unlike the SELECT and the UPDATE / DELETE clauses
    * Fix iterating or JSON-encoding a Collection without result (e.g. new Collection() returned as an empty collection): every hydrator raised a "foreach() argument must be of type array|object" warning
    * Fix UnitOfWork::pushSave() managing a new entity before its INSERT ran: saving it again after a failed INSERT (or pushing it twice before process()) ran nothing, without error, and left it without id; a new entity is now managed only once inserted (isManaged() is false until then)
    * Fix UnitOfWork::process() after a failed query: the failing entity stayed queued and the prepared statements stayed open, so every later save() / delete() on the shared UnitOfWork replayed the failed query first (silent re-INSERT, or the same error until reset()); the statements are now closed, the failing entity is unqueued (its changes are kept for a retry), the entities not processed yet stay queued, and the original exception is rethrown (not one from closing a statement that failed to prepare)
    * Fix UnitOfWork save of an entity whose setter notifies a property not mapped in the metadata: "Undefined array key" warnings then a TypeError; properties not mapped are now ignored (no UPDATE when nothing mapped changed)
    * BC Fix UnitOfWork losing the changes made in place to mutable values (a DateTime modified, a JSON object edited) without calling a setter: such a change is never notified, so the mutable fields (new field option `mutable`, by default Serializer\DateTime, Serializer\Json without `assoc`, and serializers of your own) are now written by every save of a managed entity, which therefore always runs an UPDATE; the other fields are still updated on notification only (same value as old and new value, objects included, is not a change). A mutable primary key modified in place keeps targeting its row (its database value is kept when the entity becomes managed)
    * A "datetime" field without serializer hydrates a DateTimeImmutable when its property is typed DateTimeImmutable or DateTimeInterface (same Y-m-d H:i:s format, immutable field); a property typed DateTime, or not typed, still gets a DateTime
    * Fix NotifyProperty::__serialize() and __debugInfo() losing the private properties declared in a parent or child class of the class using the trait (silent data loss for entities stored in a cache or a session); properties are now serialized with mangled names, entities serialized before are still read
    * Fix Util\PropertyAccessor::setValue() throwing a ReflectionException, without explicit setter, for a property private in a parent class or only reachable through a setter (hydration, autoincrement id); it falls back to Symfony PropertyAccess. A PSR cache hit is now kept in memory: the pool was queried again on every write
    * Docs: UPGRADE-4.0.md lists the typed extension points (loggers, entity listeners, Repository::getCollection()); the 4.0.0-rc.1 entry on serialization interfaces is corrected
    * Security: prevent SQL injection in Pgsql Driver::getInsertedIdForSequence()
    * Include 3.13.0 changes: ResetInterface on ConnectionPool, UnitOfWork and Repository (worker mode)
    * Tests: migrate from atoum to PHPUnit
    * BC Rename master/slave to primary/replica: ConnectionPool(Interface)::primary()/replica(), Connection::primary()/replica(), QueryInterface::selectPrimary(), Repository::pingPrimary(), $forceMaster parameters renamed $forcePrimary, configuration keys "primary" and "replicas"; the old methods are removed and ConnectionPool::setConfig() throws a ConfigException on the old "master" / "slaves" keys (see UPGRADE-4.0.md)
    * BC Repository::get() composite keys and the $order of Repository::getBy() take property names instead of column names, like the criteria of getBy() / getOneBy(); a column name throws a ValueException naming the property to use (see UPGRADE-4.0.md)
    * BC Values of the criteria of getBy() / getOneBy() and of get() are converted with the serializer of the field: an object (enum, DateTime, Uuid...) is serialized, an array is an IN list of converted values, or a single serialized value for a serializer implementing the new marker interface Serializer\ArrayValueInterface (Json); a non-Stringable object without serializer throws a ValueException
    * BC An empty array, or null / a nested array inside an IN list, in the criteria throws a ValueException instead of sending invalid or never-matching SQL
    * BC Empty criteria in getBy() / getOneBy(), and get([]), throw a ValueException instead of sending invalid SQL ("WHERE " without condition): use getAll() to read every row
    * BC Add the marker interface Serializer\ScalarValueInterface, implemented by Serializer\Ip and the Boolean serializers of the drivers: a scalar criterion of getBy() / getOneBy() / get() (and each scalar of an IN list) for such a field is serialized, like save() does, instead of being sent as is (getBy(['ip' => '10.0.0.1']) compared an integer column with '10.0.0.1'; false was sent as '' to PostgreSQL); a scalar converted to NULL throws a ValueException
    * BC An order direction other than ASC / DESC in Repository::getBy() throws a ValueException instead of being silently ignored
    * Fix Generator::getByCriteria() emitting an empty " ORDER BY " when every direction of the order was ignored
    * Security: Mysqli Driver::execute() quotes string values with single quotes; double quotes allowed SQL injection under the sql_mode NO_BACKSLASH_ESCAPES (real_escape_string() then only doubles single quotes) and made values identifiers under ANSI_QUOTES
    * Fix Mysqli prepared queries running on the wrong database: one driver serves every database of a server, and a statement prepared while another database was selected was reused (reads and writes went to that database, its results reported it); statements are now cached per database, closeStatement() closes the statement of every database
    * Fix startTransaction(), commit() and rollback() ignoring failures (Mysqli and Pgsql): they throw a TransactionException with the driver error, including the PostgreSQL COMMIT of an aborted transaction, which answers ROLLBACK without error; a failed commit() or rollback() leaves no transaction open
    * Fix Mysqli ping() throwing an Error ("mysqli object is not fully initialized") forever once a reconnection had failed, even after the server came back: ping() retries the connection, and queries, prepares and transactions throw a QueryException / TransactionException until it succeeds; the database, charset and timezone set meanwhile are applied on reconnection
    * Fix HydratorRelational depending on the order of the relations (since 3.x): added in another order than parent to child, it duplicated or lost the roots, left relations unset and leaked joined aliases into the rows; the relations are now sorted topologically (a setter receives entities whose relations are already set), the rows grouped by the root alias, and every source alias removed from the rows, even when its join is empty
    * Fix HydratorRelational silently dropping a relation when two relations share the same source alias (since 3.x)
    * Fix Mysqli prepared queries without parameter failing with a ValueError (bind_param() called with no type)
    * Fix the Pgsql connection string built without quoting: an empty password made libpq read the next keyword ("port=...") as the password, values with spaces, quotes or backslashes broke it, and the connect error leaked the end of a password containing a space; every value is now quoted and escaped, and the user and password are fully redacted
    * Fix Pgsql getAffectedRows() after a prepared query (PreparedQuery::getAffectedRows()): it returned the count of the last non-prepared query; the driver now reports the last query, prepared or not
    * Fix Pgsql prepared statements reused after the connection was reset (ping() re-establishing a lost connection, reconnect(), close()): the cached statements no longer existed in the new session ("prepared statement ... does not exist"); they are now forgotten and prepared again, the old ones no longer DEALLOCATE a statement of the same name in the new session and throw a QueryException if executed, and closeStatement() still accepts their names
    * Fix the Pgsql column parser of Result::setQuery(): any asterisk was rejected (COUNT(*), 2 * id), only a whole * / alias.* column is now; the columns are split, and the FROM found, outside string literals ('...', E'...', $$...$$), quoted identifiers, comments and brackets ("'from' AS kw", "name || ', ' || id" or a comment with a comma broke the columns); the columns of a WITH query are read from its main SELECT, not from the first CTE
    * BC HydratorRelational throws a HydratorException when the relations form a cycle (bidirectional relation, alias related to itself); they were partially ignored
    * Fix a cached collection without result (e.g. a cached prepared query whose statement has no result set) throwing a TypeError on a cache hit since 4.0.0-rc.1: it comes back as an empty collection
    * Fix Hydrator::objectDatabaseIs() leaking to the other aliases (since 3.x): every table first read after the alias in a row was looked up in its database
    * Fix composite primary keys in the identity map of Hydrator and HydratorRelational (since 3.x): the values were joined with "-", so ("Jean-Pierre", "Paul") and ("Jean", "Pierre-Paul") shared an entity, and Hydrator looked entities up by one primary value only (a row could get another entity, a repeated composite key never got the same one); the key now holds every primary value, without collision
    * Fix Collection::first() and count() disturbing a foreach over the same collection (the result has a single cursor): first() inside the loop restarted it forever, count() on a cached collection ended it; first() returns the first item of the last iteration, CacheResult::getNumRows() counts without moving the cursor
    * BC Serializer\DateTimeImmutable (datetime_immutable fields) writes Y-m-d H:i:s by default instead of ATOM, and could not read a MySQL DATETIME / PostgreSQL timestamp without a format option; Serializer\DateTime and Serializer\DateTimeImmutable now read a value that does not match their format with the PHP date parser (ATOM values written by the old default, PostgreSQL timestamptz...), and reject an empty string instead of reading it as the current time with unSerializeUseFormat false
    * Fix Serializer\BackedEnum::unserialize() on an int-backed enum: a value that is not an integer ('abc', '') threw a TypeError instead of a Serializer\RuntimeException, and '1.5' returned the case 1 with a deprecation; only integers and integer strings are accepted
    * Fix Serializer\Json::serialize() throwing with the JSON_PARTIAL_OUTPUT_ON_ERROR option: the partial output is returned
    * Fix Serializer\DateTime and Serializer\DateTimeImmutable reading a format without time (e.g. Y-m-d for a DATE column) with the current time of day: the fields missing from the format are reset (midnight)
    * Fix setTimezone() (Mysqli and Pgsql) silently ignoring a timezone rejected by the server while recording it as current: it throws a DriverException with the database error and the timezone is not recorded; a timezone rejected when ping() / reconnect() applies it again is forgotten (the session keeps the server default) and the next setTimezone() reports it. Mysqli sends the timezone as a single-quoted, escaped string: double-quoted, it was read as an identifier under the sql_mode ANSI_QUOTES
    * Fix Pgsql failed queries raising a PHP warning before Ting's exception: with an error handler converting warnings to exceptions (Symfony debug), an ErrorException escaped instead of the QueryException / TransactionException / DriverException, and the query log was never stopped; pg_query(), pg_query_params(), pg_prepare(), pg_execute() and pg_connect() are silenced, the query log is stopped whatever happens, prepare() without connection no longer starts it, the DEALLOCATE of a statement destructor no longer raises a warning, and setCharset() without connection throws a DriverException instead of an Error
    * Fix Mysqli prepare() leaving the query log started when the prepare fails (Pgsql stops it); the log of queries, prepares and statement executions is now stopped also when mysqli throws (report mode MYSQLI_REPORT_ERROR). Fix getInsertedId() and getAffectedRows() throwing an Error after a failed reconnection: they throw a QueryException, like the queries
    * Fix SphinxQL query parameters: null was sent as '' (with a "Passing null to parameter" deprecation) and false as ''; values are now quoted as with Mysqli, null as NULL and booleans as 0 / 1
    * Fix ConnectionPool sharing one driver between connections that differ: the key joined host, port, user and password with "|" (user "a|b" with password "c" collided with user "a" with password "b|c", a null user or password with an empty one) and ignored the driver class (a Mysqli and a SphinxQL connection to the same host, port and credentials got the driver of whichever was created first); Driver::getConnectionKey() now serializes the values (Pgsql still includes the database) and ConnectionPool keys the drivers by class too
    * Fix Util\Debug::export(): dates were exported without their value, unlike 3.x (now with their date and timezone, other internal objects with what var_dump() shows), a negative $maxDepth on a cycle recursed until memory ran out, the private properties of parent classes were missing, generators were consumed (no longer iterated) and a write-only virtual hooked property threw an Error (virtual properties are skipped)
    * Fix the INSERT of an entity whose typed property read by a custom getter is not initialized: the getter was called and threw an Error ("must not be accessed before initialization"); the field is skipped, as with a conventional getter
    * Fix Hydrator::mapObjectTo() with a null joined entity (LEFT JOIN without match) depending on the order of the columns (since 3.x): when the columns of $from came after those of $to, the method received an entity whose properties were all null and the row got the $from key back, set to null; the method is now never called for a null entity, and $from is always removed from the row
    * Fix UnitOfWork::manage() adding its property listener on every call (each delete then insert of the same entity added one more, and every change was then notified once per listener); the listener is added once per entity, and the changes of an entity not managed (detached, or new) are no longer recorded
    * Fix UnitOfWork::pushDelete() of an entity never inserted (not managed and without primary key, or pushed with pushSave() before in the same process()) running "DELETE ... WHERE key IS NULL"; it is unqueued without query (an entity not managed but with its primary key is still deleted by that key)
    * Fix HydratorAggregator losing every row (no group, and a PHP 8.5 "Using null as an array offset" deprecation) when the callable given to callableIdIs() returns null; it throws a HydratorException, a group identifier is required
    * BC Fix the hydrator choosing the metadata of a table by registration order (since 3.x): when several metadata share a table on a connection (one per database or schema) and none matches the database and schema of the result, it took the first registered; it now takes the only one registered, else the only one of the same database, else the only one of the same schema, and otherwise throws a HydratorException naming the candidates (use Hydrator::objectDatabaseIs() / objectSchemaIs()). Schemas are compared case-insensitively when no exact match: Pgsql\Result lowercases the schemas read in the query, so a metadata with a mixed-case schema (mySchema) was never matched
    * Fix PreparedQuery and Cached\PreparedQuery keeping the connection they were first prepared on: a query read on a replica then executed ran the write on the replica, and selectPrimary(true) after a first read kept reading the replica; the statement is now prepared again when the target connection (primary for execute() or selectPrimary(true), replica otherwise) changes
    * Fix Mysqli and Pgsql drivers keeping a transaction open across a reconnection: after a connection lost in a transaction and re-established by ping() or reconnect(), startTransaction() threw "Cannot start another transaction" and commit() "succeeded" on the new connection although the server had rolled back the writes; when the connection is replaced or closed (reconnect(), a failed Mysqli reconnection, a Pgsql ping() resetting the connection, close()), the transaction is now marked as lost: the next commit() throws a TransactionException, rollback() succeeds without sending anything, startTransaction() works again
    * BC Native types on every parameter, return value and property (PHPStan type coverage at 100%): SerializeInterface::serialize() and UnserializeInterface::unserialize() take and return mixed (an implementation must declare a return type), CollectionFactoryInterface::get() returns Collection, CollectionInterface::first() returns mixed and setFromCache() takes a bool, Repository::get() / getOneBy() return ?object, Metadata::createEntity() returns object and getRepository() ?string, the remaining protected properties are typed (ConnectionPool, MetadataRepository, drivers, Query, Metadata, Repository), and the values cast before (Cached\Query::setTtl() / setForce(), Hydrator::objectDatabaseIs() / objectSchemaIs()...) are typed instead; the native extension handles (mysqli, PgSql) are typed object; see UPGRADE-4.0.md
    * Fix Mysqli Driver::execute() without collection throwing a TypeError since 4.0.0-rc.1 when the result set has no row; it returns null again, as in 3.x
    * Fix Query::query() throwing a TypeError since 4.0.0-rc.1 for a statement without result set on Mysqli (the driver returns true instead of the collection); it returns its collection, as PreparedQuery::query()
    * Fix Mysqli Driver::reconnect() called before connect() (since 3.x): it raised "Undefined array key" warnings then opened a connection with the default parameters of mysqli; it throws a NeverConnectedException, as ping()
    * PHPDoc fully typed for static analysis (generics and array shapes, see UPGRADE-4.0.md): Repository<T>, CollectionInterface<T>, HydratorInterface<T>, QueryInterface<T>; PHPStan no longer ignores missing iterable value types and generics
    * Fix Mysqli and Pgsql drivers when the parameters of a query cannot be parsed (PCRE failure, e.g. pcre.backtrack_limit reached on a huge query): execute() and prepare() throw a QueryException instead of sending a null query on (deprecation, then an empty query or a TypeError)
    * Fix Mysqli Driver when mysqli_init() fails: the constructor throws a DriverException instead of leaving a driver without connection (an Error on the first call), reconnect() returns false instead of reconnecting the dropped connection
    * Fix Mysqli Result::getNumRows() and Pgsql Result without result (setResult() not called): no row, as the Mysqli iteration, instead of an Error or a TypeError; Pgsql Result::setQuery() before setResult() throws a QueryException
    * Fix Pgsql Statement::execute() before setConnection() and setCollectionWithResult() before setQuery(): they throw a QueryException instead of a TypeError
    * Fix the hydrators iterated without result (setResult() not called): they yield nothing, as count() gives 0, instead of raising a "foreach() argument must be of type array|object" warning
    * Fix Hydrator and its subclasses on a row of a result without connection name or database, and before setMetadataRepository() or setUnitOfWork() (set by the CollectionFactory): they throw a HydratorException instead of a TypeError or an Error
    * Fix Query::query() and its subclasses without collection on a query built without collection factory, and Cached\Query::query() / Cached\PreparedQuery::query() before setCache(): they throw a QueryException instead of an Error
    * Fix Metadata used before setConnectionName() / setDatabase() (getConnection(), so a Repository) or setTable() (the generated queries): it throws a ConfigException instead of a TypeError
    * Fix MetadataRepository::findMetadataForEntity() on an unknown entity without callbackNotFound: it does nothing, as findMetadataForRepository(), instead of throwing an Error
    * Add Connection::getName()
    * Fix Pgsql Driver::reconnect() before connect() connecting with libpq's default settings (empty connection string): it throws a NeverConnectedException, like Mysqli

4.0.0-rc.1 (2025-12-15):
    * BC PHP 8.0 dropped, minimum version is now PHP 8.1
    * BC All classes now fully typehinted with strict types and return types
    * BC Pgsql Driver now uses native PHP 8.1+ PgSql\Connection and PgSql\Result classes instead of resources
    * Serializers typehinted (SerializeInterface and UnserializeInterface keep their 3.x signatures: the native return types were removed before this release)
    * BC Added ping() and setTimezone() methods to DriverInterface
    * BC Added ConnectionPoolInterface::setDatabaseOptions() method
    * BC Deleted Metadata::getGetter() and Metadata::getSetter() methods
    * BC Deleted deprecated getInsertId() methods on Mysqli and Pgsql drivers (use getInsertedId() instead)
    * BC Deleted deprecated getInsertIdForSequence() on Pgsql driver (use getInsertedIdForSequence() instead)
    * BC Deleted deprecated getInsertId() on QueryInterface and Query class (use getInsertedId() instead)
    * BC Deleted Generator::getByCriteriaWithOrderAndLimit(), merged into Generator::getByCriteria() with $order and $limit parameters
    * BC Deleted UnitOfWork::generateUid() and UnitOfWork::generateUUID() methods
    * New feature: HydratorValueObject allows hydrating simple objects without metadata using native fetch_object() methods
    * New feature: ResultInterface::setObjectToFetch() for value object hydration (corrected entry: no fetchObject() method was ever exposed; setObjectToFetch() was removed in 4.0.0, see above)
    * Improvement: UnitOfWork now uses WeakMap exclusively for internal entity storage (enhanced from PHP 8.0 implementation)
    * Improvement: PHPStan analysis raised to level 7 with baseline significantly reduced (from ~2200 to <50 errors)
    * Improvement: Type coverage tool added (tomasvotruba/type-coverage) with minimum thresholds: 97% return types, 85% param types, 83% property types
    * Improvement: Rector configuration added for automated refactoring and code quality improvements (targeting PHP 8.0+)
    * Improvement: PHPStan custom extension for properties (CCMBenchmark\Ting\PHPStan\PropertiesExtension)

3.15.0 (2026-10-05):
    * Repository::get() (composite primary key), getBy() / getOneBy() criteria and the getBy() order now all take
      property names, converted to column names by the Metadata
    * Deprecate column names in these keys: a key that is not a property but is the column of a field still works
      and triggers a silenced E_USER_DEPRECATED. A key that is both a property and the column of another field is
      the property
    * Deprecate order directions other than ASC / DESC (case-insensitive): still ignored, they trigger a silenced
      E_USER_DEPRECATED and will throw a ValueException in 4.0. An order whose directions are all ignored no longer
      produces an invalid "ORDER BY" clause
    * Criteria values (getBy(), getOneBy() and get()) are converted by the serializer of their field:
        * an object is serialized (enum, DateTime, Uuid...); an object for a field without serializer throws a
          ValueException, except a Stringable object which is still sent as is
        * an array becomes an IN list of converted values, an empty array throws a ValueException
          (it produced an invalid "IN ()" before), check it first: if ($ids === []) { return ...; }
        * an array for a field whose serializer implements the new Serializer\ArrayValueInterface (Json does) is
          serialized as a whole and compared with "=". The result depends on the column type: a TEXT column matches
          when the encoding is the same, a MySQL JSON column compared to a string never matches, PostgreSQL has no
          "=" operator for json (jsonb has one)
        * null (IS NULL) and scalars are unchanged

3.14.0 (2026-10-05):
    * Security: prevent SQL injection in Pgsql Driver::getInsertedIdForSequence() (backport from 4.0.0-rc.1)
    * Drop Symfony 6 and PHP 8.1 support, PHP >= 8.2 is now required
    * Add Symfony 8 support
    * Tests: migrate from atoum to PHPUnit
    * Add primary/replica names: ConnectionPool::primary() / replica(), Connection::primary() / replica(),
      Query::selectPrimary() and Repository::pingPrimary()
    * Connection configuration now uses the "primary" and "replicas" keys
    * Deprecate ConnectionPool::master() / slave(), Connection::master() / slave(), Query::selectMaster()
      and Repository::pingMaster(): they trigger a silenced E_USER_DEPRECATED and delegate to the new methods
    * Deprecate the "master" and "slaves" connection configuration keys: they trigger a silenced E_USER_DEPRECATED
      and are converted to "primary" / "replicas" (the new key wins when both are given)
    * ConnectionPoolInterface::master() / slave() are deprecated, they will be replaced by primary() / replica() in 4.0.
      Connection uses primary() / replica() when the pool provides them, master() / slave() otherwise
    * Fix Cached\PreparedQuery: selectPrimary() (formerly selectMaster()) is now honoured for reading queries

3.13.0 (2026-09-24):
    * Drop PHP 8.0 support, PHP >= 8.1 is now required
    * Add ResetInterface on ConnectionPool, UnitOfWork and Repository to reset state between requests (worker mode)

3.12.1 (2025-12-16):
